% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api_router.py` as the Replaces the exact-match chain at playlist_editor.py:1262-1414. register(pattern, methods, handler) and route(method, path) with <param> segments; match on the urlparse()d path, never on raw self.path, or a query string defeats every pattern. ALL 25 EXISTING ROUTES MUST STILL RESOLVE UNCHANGED, which makes this the highest-regression-risk change in the feature. MATCHING RULE: segments are scored per position and a LITERAL SEGMENT OUTRANKS A <param> SEGMENT AT THE SAME POSITION REGARDLESS OF REGISTRATION ORDER; the highest-scoring pattern wins. Without this rule, registration order silently decides whether GET /api/plans/active reaches module 19 or is swallowed by module 20's <slug> and 404s on an unknown plan. Ties are impossible because two identical patterns cannot both register. Unknown path -> 404. Wrong method -> 405 WITH AN Allow HEADER naming the registered methods for that pattern; MDN documents the header as mandatory on 405, this module already knows the methods so emitting it is free, and without it an agent harness cannot tell a typo'd path from a wrong verb. A handler raising StalePlanError is translated HERE to 409 with the conflict payload in the body, so no individual route repeats it.

